 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Yes.** In the RBA's advertised rates for September 2026 (latest), the standard variable rate for investors is **9.35%** and for owner-occupiers it is **8.77%**, a gap of **0.58 percentage points**.\n\nThe gap has been roughly the same for years:\n\n| Period | Owner-occupier standard variable | Investor standard variable | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Jan 2019 | 5.37% | 5.94% | 0.57 pp |\n| Apr 2022 | 4.52% | 5.10% | 0.58 pp |\n| Dec 2024 | 8.77% | 9.35% | 0.58 pp |\n| Sep 2026 | 8.77% | 9.35% | 0.58 pp |\n\nBoth rates have moved with the cash rate, but the premium for investors has stayed close to 0.6 points throughout.\n\nDiscounted variable loans show a smaller gap. In September 2026 the investor discounted rate was 7.13% and the owner-occupier rate was 6.80%, a gap of 0.33 points.\n\nThese are advertised rates. The RBA notes that rates actually paid on new loans are lower, and the RBA's table F6 has those figures if you want what borrowers actually pay.",
